            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0405" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/8–2548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-08-28T12:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1242. Please deliver personally following message to Foreign Minister from me in
                    reply to his message forwarded in urtel 1576 August 25: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Thank you for your message forwarded to me by Ambassador Stuart. I have
                            just received information regarding the emergency financial and economic
                            measures proclaimed by President Chiang and am now having a careful
                            study made of them. I am gratified at your <pb facs="0406" n="396"
                                xml:id="pg396"/> determination, as well as that of your colleagues,
                            to enforce measures designed to help meet China’s serious economic
                            problems and view sympathetically measures of self-help taken by the
                            Chinese Government.</p>
                        <p>I look forward to seeing you at the UN Assembly in Paris and to having
                            the opportunity of discussions on these and several other matters. My
                            warm regards to you.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
